# A rule about where this program may reach. The checker reads the rule; the
# program never does. The boundary here is a network one — usage data may go to
# the first-party endpoint and nowhere else. The fetch below stays inside that
# line, so the checker passes it: the rule documents the intent and guards
# against a later edit that would quietly cross it.

rule [first-party-only] anything may not ask to "https://third-party.example.com"
  because "usage data must not leave the first-party boundary"

note:
  from "data-handling policy, section 4"
  derives-from [first-party-only]

use http

let stats = ask "https://metrics.example.com/report"
  or fail as metrics-unavailable

show "usage reported to the first-party endpoint"
